Bash is denied in this session (don't-ask mode), so I can't run `digest`. I did not try to work around it.

The digest needs three things that depend on Bash:
- **Resolving the vault and date.** It runs `wiki_vault.py` and `wiki_tool.py` through `uv run --script`, and it needs `TZ=Pacific/Auckland date`.
- **Enumerating notes.** It has to scan `10_Sources/`, `30_Concepts/` and `40_Guides/` for notes with and without `af_targets`. I have no Glob or Grep tool here.
- **The `af-tag` pre-step.** It needs those listings and a post-edit frontmatter check before the digest is written.

Nothing was written or changed.

To fix this, allow Bash in the headless runner's permission settings. `uv run --script ~/.claude/skills/wiki/scripts/*`, `git -C <vault> status`, and `date` would cover it. Alternatively, run the digest interactively. Then re-run `/wiki-agents digest --headless`.

